"Ha!" Hadrik chuckles, wincing as his split lip pulls against his swollen cheek. "I'd pay good gold to see Gontrok's face when he realizes he was yanked away for a faulty wire."

"We cannot linger here," Daren says. He drags his sword up from the flagstones, leaning heavily on the hilt before limping toward us. "The royal guards may be gone, but regular city patrols will flood this square any second. We need cover to rest and patch ourselves up."

